          organizer,
        })} />
        <hr>
      </li>

      <li>
        <h2>
          <a href="https://www.tickettailor.com/events/thetextilebuffet/2487768?date=2026-11-15" target="_blank">
            14.-15.11.2026 LOOPTOPIA @ à la mode, Berlin
          </a>
        </h2>
        <div class="flex-has-logos">
          <MapMarkerIcon />
          <a href="https://www.google.com/maps?cid=0x47a84e2c3519b647:0xe30ca61524a7c89e" target="_blank">
            Sat 14 + Sun 15 November 2026<br>
            à la mode Schneiderei und Atelier, Aufbau Haus, Prinzenstraße 85 C, 10969 Berlin
          </a>
        </div>

        <ul>
          <li>Saturday 14 November 4 - 5:30 p.m.</li>
          <li>Saturday 14 November 6 - 7:30 p.m.</li>
          <li>Sunday 15 November 2 - 3:30 p.m.</li>
          <li>Sunday 15 November 4 - 5:30 p.m.</li>
        </ul>

        <a class="buttonlike float-right" href="https://www.tickettailor.com/events/thetextilebuffet/2487768?date=2026-11-15" target="_blank">get your ticket</a>

        <h3 style="text-transform: uppercase">Safety Pin Revival: from useful to iconic, and back again.</h3>
        <p>
          The safety pin has seen a lot. It started as a practical everyday helper, present in every sewing or travel kit, to become a rebellious symbol of punk culture and has been revisited by many Fashion creators.
        </p>
        <p>
          For LOOPTOPIA Berlin 2026, THE TEXTILE BUFFET gives this small all-rounder a fresh take.
        </p>
        <p>
          We set up an abundant table at à la mode, where you'll find lace, velvet ribbons, sequins, buttons, found pieces and fabric scraps, including materials straight from the tailoring studio. We invite you to play with colours, shapes and textures, to create your special safety pin.
        </p>
        <p>
          Worn as an accessory for your jacket, coat or bag. It can give your garment garment a new accent, or help cover a small flaw. Cherry on top of the cake? Whenever you need the safety pin for something else entirely, you already have it with you.
        </p>
        <p>
          THE TEXTILE BUFFET is a natural fit for LOOPTOPIA, the Weekend of events dedicated to the circular economy: we work with what already exists, rediscover materials and show how small changes can spark the desire to keep wearing our clothes for longer, and in new ways.
        </p>
        <p>
          For this public edition, we've created an inclusive format: a 90-minute sitting for only €15.
        </p>
        <p>
          No prior experience needed. Curiosity and a wish to try things out are all you need.
        </p>

        What's included:<br>
        <br>
        <ul>
          <li>90 minutes at the makers' table</li>
          <li>All materials and tools provided</li>
          <li>Leave with your own one-of-one safety pin, made by your own hands</li>
        </ul>

        <p><b>Price:</b> € 15,- per person</p>
        <p><b>Spots:</b> Limited to 12 people per session.</p>

        <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "Event",
          "name": "The TEXTILE BUFFET SAFETY PIN REVIVAL",
          "startDate": "2026-11-24T16:00:00+02:00",
          "endDate": "2026-11-15T17:30:00+02:00",
